00:04:14.976 --> 00:04:16.043
- [Voiceover] Sky asks,

00:04:16.043 --> 00:04:18.146
"Adele's new album isn't
streaming anywhere.

00:04:18.146 --> 00:04:20.363
"Is she romantic about selling albums,

00:04:20.363 --> 00:04:23.845
"or leveraging people to buy music?"

00:04:23.845 --> 00:04:26.104
- Oh, wait a minute,
Staphon's just standing here,

00:04:26.104 --> 00:04:28.181
and if you're just, I
mean, show that, DRock.

00:04:28.181 --> 00:04:29.773
He's really, truly just standing here.

00:04:29.773 --> 00:04:30.750
(laughter)

00:04:30.750 --> 00:04:33.663
One of the things that makes me unhappy,

00:04:33.663 --> 00:04:35.115
I mean, really, I know
you've gotta watch it

00:04:35.115 --> 00:04:36.460
for editing purposes,

00:04:36.460 --> 00:04:38.481
but you should be

00:04:38.481 --> 00:04:41.558
you should be doing something, Staphon.

00:04:41.558 --> 00:04:42.835
- [Staphon] You're right.
(laughter)

00:04:42.835 --> 00:04:44.855
- So let's do a little Periscoping.

00:04:44.855 --> 00:04:46.503
Alright.

00:04:46.503 --> 00:04:49.324
Adele's new album is not
streaming anywhere, right?

00:04:49.324 --> 00:04:51.308
- [India] Is she romantic
about selling albums,

00:04:51.308 --> 00:04:54.090
or leveraging people to buy music?

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:56.550
- It's a really good
question, and the truth is,

00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:58.710
there's a time and a place
for you to do everything,

00:04:58.710 --> 00:05:01.367
so, we talk about spec work here, right?

00:05:01.367 --> 00:05:02.853
DRock got his job on it, right?

00:05:02.853 --> 00:05:04.467
Like, you do something for free

00:05:04.467 --> 00:05:06.650
and it leads to what you want to happen.

00:05:06.650 --> 00:05:11.260
Well look, when you're
Jay-Z in the early days

00:05:11.260 --> 00:05:13.756
and nobody knows who the hell you are,

00:05:13.756 --> 00:05:15.881
it makes sense to go to a club,

00:05:15.881 --> 00:05:18.133
not get paid, and spit your fire,

00:05:18.133 --> 00:05:19.398
because you're building leverage.

00:05:19.398 --> 00:05:22.466
I used to go and speak for free.

00:05:22.466 --> 00:05:23.516
Often.

00:05:23.516 --> 00:05:25.138
I don't do that anymore.

00:05:25.138 --> 00:05:26.322
Because I have an alternative.

00:05:26.322 --> 00:05:28.467
I have demand now.

00:05:28.467 --> 00:05:31.926
Adele, if her name was "Shmadele,"

00:05:31.926 --> 00:05:35.561
if Shmadele came out with a new album

00:05:35.561 --> 00:05:38.265
and nobody knows who Shmadele is,

00:05:38.265 --> 00:05:40.101
I would hope, I don't
follow music enough, so,

00:05:40.101 --> 00:05:41.680
if there's a Shmadele, I apologize.

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:43.966
But if you're Shmadele and
nobody knows who you are,

00:05:43.966 --> 00:05:46.717
you not only want to be
on streaming services,

00:05:46.717 --> 00:05:48.899
you wanna, like, show up on
Instagram people's accounts

00:05:48.899 --> 00:05:50.303
and, like, sing, you wanna, like,

00:05:50.303 --> 00:05:52.824
go outside and give
people your free album,

00:05:52.824 --> 00:05:55.122
like, you want exposure
because that creates leverage

00:05:55.122 --> 00:05:56.898
that you then can charge for.

00:05:56.898 --> 00:05:58.280
Adele doesn't have that problem,

00:05:58.280 --> 00:06:02.517
and so she's trying to maximize
profits through that channel

00:06:02.517 --> 00:06:04.758
versus the pennies that streaming does.

00:06:04.758 --> 00:06:06.280
It does two things:

00:06:06.280 --> 00:06:07.619
it makes her more money,

00:06:07.619 --> 00:06:10.138
it gives her less exposure by accident

00:06:10.138 --> 00:06:12.402
for people that could find her

00:06:12.402 --> 00:06:14.340
through Spotify or other places

00:06:14.340 --> 00:06:16.244
that have never discovered her before.

00:06:16.244 --> 00:06:19.519
From my point of view,
it's a fine balancing act.

00:06:19.519 --> 00:06:20.458
Right?

00:06:20.458 --> 00:06:21.421
I think if you look at the people

00:06:21.421 --> 00:06:24.336
that pushed against Napster,
or pushed against technology,

00:06:24.336 --> 00:06:27.621
the bands that pushed
against MTV, historically,

00:06:27.621 --> 00:06:29.236
that didn't make music videos,

00:06:29.236 --> 00:06:33.763
if you're too romantic for
too long, you can get caught,

00:06:33.763 --> 00:06:35.980
unless you're in the top 1%.

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:38.336
I believe that there's an absolute way

00:06:38.336 --> 00:06:42.042
to not conform to modern marketing.

00:06:42.042 --> 00:06:43.329
A€ la Apple.

00:06:43.329 --> 00:06:45.768
If your product is
disproportionately the best,

00:06:45.768 --> 00:06:48.902
consistently, you can get
away with acting differently.

00:06:48.902 --> 00:06:50.260
But if you look, even at, like,

00:06:50.260 --> 00:06:51.560
actors at the top of their game,

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:52.629
like a Will Smith

00:06:52.629 --> 00:06:54.904
who made the same kind
of movie for a while,

00:06:54.904 --> 00:06:56.819
everybody has their day and time.

00:06:56.819 --> 00:06:59.862
And so my answer is, if
Adele has this read properly

00:06:59.862 --> 00:07:02.646
that she doesn't need more
exposure, she has a huge fanbase,

00:07:02.646 --> 00:07:04.760
she just put out fire,

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:06.408
and it killed, cool.

00:07:06.408 --> 00:07:08.161
Look at Justin Bieber in parallel.

00:07:08.161 --> 00:07:10.182
Did a lot of marketing,
a lot of Instagram,

00:07:10.182 --> 00:07:12.480
a lot of releasing, a
lot of stuff out there,

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:14.222
and it really worked.

00:07:14.222 --> 00:07:15.684
Now the question becomes,

00:07:15.684 --> 00:07:18.239
he needed that because he
was in this funny spot,

00:07:18.239 --> 00:07:20.715
does he do the same thing next time?

00:07:20.715 --> 00:07:22.469
Or does he go a little bit
closer to where Adele is

00:07:22.469 --> 00:07:23.989
if Adele's over here?

00:07:23.989 --> 00:07:25.568
The answer to the
question, my friends, is,

00:07:25.568 --> 00:07:26.811
there's no absolutes.

00:07:26.811 --> 00:07:27.913
There is no right answer.

00:07:27.913 --> 00:07:30.455
There's moments in time,
like the first question.

00:07:30.455 --> 00:07:32.812
There's knowing what to do at this moment.

00:07:32.812 --> 00:07:35.633
The things I do running
this business at 600 people

00:07:35.633 --> 00:07:37.827
is very different than what I did at four.

00:07:37.827 --> 00:07:40.636
I don't say yes, I said
no to 19 deals today.

00:07:40.636 --> 00:07:42.611
I said yes to every deal
when we first started.

00:07:42.611 --> 00:07:43.794
Right?

00:07:43.794 --> 00:07:45.813
And so we just talked about,

00:07:45.813 --> 00:07:47.266
we just all got together on my team

00:07:47.266 --> 00:07:49.274
to talk about how much
book-buying you have to do

00:07:49.274 --> 00:07:51.375
for all my packages for the next book.

00:07:51.375 --> 00:07:52.408
I think we can all agree,

00:07:52.408 --> 00:07:54.265
there's a lot more books
that you need to do

00:07:54.265 --> 00:07:55.949
to do the things that I did two years ago

00:07:55.949 --> 00:07:57.446
for Jab, Jab, Jab, Right Hook.

00:07:57.446 --> 00:07:59.014
'Cause I'm busier, I
have more opportunities.

00:07:59.014 --> 00:08:00.048
I have more leverage.

00:08:00.048 --> 00:08:02.670
This is where the #AskGaryVee
show's brand, right,

00:08:02.670 --> 00:08:03.565
has helped me.

00:08:03.565 --> 00:08:04.306
Why don't you say,

00:08:04.306 --> 00:08:05.601
I mean, you're just, this is amazing,

00:08:05.601 --> 00:08:06.703
but why don't you just say hello.

00:08:06.703 --> 00:08:07.593
- Hi.

00:08:07.593 --> 00:08:08.916
- [Gary] Tell the Vayner
Nation who you are.

00:08:08.916 --> 00:08:11.447
- Uh, Reed Adler, sound guy.

00:08:11.447 --> 00:08:13.153
- Yeah, so Reed just was working

00:08:13.153 --> 00:08:14.209
on something else I just did,

00:08:14.209 --> 00:08:14.976
he's just hanging out,

00:08:14.976 --> 00:08:16.428
he said before we aired,

00:08:16.428 --> 00:08:17.971
"hey, my brother turned
me on to the show,"

00:08:17.971 --> 00:08:21.187
his brother and him now know who I am more

00:08:21.187 --> 00:08:22.348
than they did before

00:08:22.348 --> 00:08:23.508
because this show's working for me,

00:08:23.508 --> 00:08:24.449
which then gave me leverage

00:08:24.449 --> 00:08:26.748
to ask for 3,500 books to give a keynote,

00:08:26.748 --> 00:08:28.350
versus 2,000 books.

00:08:28.350 --> 00:08:29.673
So this is how it works, guys.

00:08:29.673 --> 00:08:31.554
You put in the work for a year and a half,

00:08:31.554 --> 00:08:32.865
you build up leverage,

00:08:32.865 --> 00:08:34.827
which then allows you to get more stuff.

00:08:34.827 --> 00:08:37.532
So Adele's move, where a
lot of people might say,

00:08:37.532 --> 00:08:39.030
"oh, Gary's gonna say,"

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:39.971
because I know a lot of you thought this,

00:08:39.971 --> 00:08:41.452
"oh, that's bad, you're killing exposure."

00:08:41.452 --> 00:08:43.727
No, it's balancing that.

00:08:43.727 --> 00:08:47.035
What's important is not
reading your own headlines

00:08:47.035 --> 00:08:49.415
and doing the thing that Adele's doing

00:08:49.415 --> 00:08:52.085
too long, too many times in a row

00:08:52.085 --> 00:08:53.953
that now no 17-year-old in America

00:08:53.953 --> 00:08:55.793
or 15-year-old even knows who you are,

00:08:55.793 --> 00:08:58.115
because they only live in those platforms.

00:08:58.115 --> 00:08:59.009
Right?

00:08:59.009 --> 00:09:00.655
All the bands that said no

00:09:00.655 --> 00:09:03.954
to being the music on John Madden Football

00:09:03.954 --> 00:09:08.749
in 1999, 2001, 2004, 2006,

00:09:08.749 --> 00:09:11.737
they missed out on being Good Charlotte.

00:09:11.737 --> 00:09:13.141
Good Charlotte said yes,

00:09:13.141 --> 00:09:14.513
they were willing to give away the music,

00:09:14.513 --> 00:09:17.603
or go find out how the
Black Eyed Peas worked.

00:09:17.603 --> 00:09:18.765
Will.i.am was smart, he's like,

00:09:18.765 --> 00:09:19.890
"oh, for a TV commercial?

00:09:19.890 --> 00:09:21.690
For this Apple iPod thing?

00:09:21.690 --> 00:09:23.930
Okay. We won't be too fancy."

00:09:23.930 --> 00:09:25.672
And the three big bands
that you've heard of

00:09:25.672 --> 00:09:26.891
that said no

00:09:26.891 --> 00:09:29.062
missed the chance of being huge.

00:09:29.062 --> 00:09:32.107
So yo, I even say yes to things for free,

00:09:32.107 --> 00:09:36.311
if the exposure is
disproportionately unbelievable.

00:09:36.311 --> 00:09:38.021
Saturday Night Live
does not need to pay me

00:09:38.021 --> 00:09:41.086
to show up and be in an SNL.

